rk">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><section class="hero"><div class="hero-topline"><span>PHANG NGA, THAILAND</span><span>Stories of the City / Issue 1</span></div><div class="hero-layout"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="hero-eyebrow"><i></i> An old town guide that invites you to walk slowly</span><h1>Takua Pa<span class="hero-title-bottom">A storytelling city<em>101</em></span></h1><p>Through shrine doors, looking at old house windows<br>And know the city a bit more at every stop</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#places">Choose your destination<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span class="tiny-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>20 Places · 7 Traditions · 59 Shops<br>Compiled from Takua Pa municipal brochure</span></div></div><div class="hero-collage"><div class="collage-ring" aria-hidden="true"></div><span class="stamp">TAKUA PA<br><strong>Takua Pa</strong><br>OLD TOWN</span><a class="postcard postcard-main" href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="eager"><span><b>01 / Old buildings</b> Tao Ming School ↗</span></a><a class="postcard postcard-left" href="/en/places/guan-yu/"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"><span>Community faith ↗</span></a><a class="postcard postcard-right" href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"><span>A window into the past ↗</span></a><span class="collage-note">Collect stories along the way</span><span class="collage-spark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></div></div><div class="hero-bottom"><span>Temples & Pagodas</span><i>✳</i><span>Shrine</span><i>✳</i><span>Old house</span><i>✳</i><span>Riverside market</span><a href="#start">Start reading ↓</a></div></section><nav class="quick-start" aria-label="เริ่มต้นใช้งาน"><h2 class="visually-hidden">Start Here</h2><a class="quick-card" href="/en/map/" data-qs="map"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Open Map</b><small>See what is where</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/places/" data-qs="places"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Where to go</b><small>20 places in the old town</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/eat/" data-qs="eat"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>What to eat</b><small>60 shops in the area</small></span></a><a class="quick-card" href="/en/trip/" data-qs="trip"><span class="qs-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="qs-text"><b>Plan my trip</b><small>Save places and follow the route</small></span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav><section id="start" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">01 / Read the town</span><h2>Start from your interests</h2></div><p>Three routes to read the city · Choose stops in your own way</p></div><div class="route-cards"><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-1"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/wat-boromthat.webp" alt="วัดบรมธาตุคีรีเขต (วัดลุ่ม)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">01</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Read the city through faith</span><h3>Temples and Pagodas Route</h3><span class="route-footer">6 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-2"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">02</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Look at the story of the Chinese community</span><h3>Shrines and Vegetarian Halls Route</h3><span class="route-footer">4 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-3"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">03</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Trace buildings, trade, and people</span><h3>Old Buildings and Riverside Market Route</h3><span class="route-footer">6 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a><a class="route-card" href="/en/routes/#route-4"><div class="route-art"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="route-no">04</span></div><div class="route-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Best for a half-day visit</span><h3>Short walk from wooden house</h3><span class="route-footer">4 destinations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a></div></section><section class="section city-feed" id="city-feed"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">02 / Read the town</span><h2>City topics and news</h2></div><p>Compiled stories and the latest updates in Takua Pa</p></div><div class="city-feed-grid"><div class="cf-stories"><h3 class="cf-title">Stories of the City</h3><div class="story-tiles"><a class="story-tile story-tile-lead" href="/en/stories/city/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/riverwalk.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Know the city</span><b>Takua Pa: The Town That Moved with the River</b><p>From an ancient settlement on the trans-peninsular route to a market and mining town · Verified facts and questions waiting to be answered.</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/architecture/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Old houses and architecture</span><b>Buildings built with tin money and dredger steel · Architecture that remembers the town</b><p>Read Takua Pa through the shophouses on Culture Street, Boon Sung Iron Bridge, the governor's residence, and Tao Ming School · The transition embedded in brick, mortar, and steel structures</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/water-trade/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">Waterways and trade</span><b>From Thung Tuk to the Takua Pa River: The Day the Waterway Built the Town</b><p>The river is not just a backdrop. It is a route, a connector of people, and the determiner of the town's fate, which had to relocate due to sedimentation.</p><small>7 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/food-people/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">People and flavors</span><b>Flavours of the Baba Community and the Old Market</b><p>Food serves as both household memories and evidence of cultural exchange · Read Takua Pa through the Baba cuisine, double-layered Tao Sor, and the Culture Street</p><small>7 minutes</small></span></a><a class="story-tile" href="/en/stories/kuapapoh/"><span class="sc-img"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sc-body"><span class="chapter">City topics</span><b>Kuapapoh: The Day Old Houses Stand Up to Tell Their Stories</b><p>A creative space project that revived houses number 78, 109, and 305 · What the new generation tells about the town, and what history still needs to uncover</p><small>6 minutes</small></span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/stories/">Read all stories ↗</a></div><div class="cf-news"><h3 class="cf-title">Latest Updates</h3><ol class="news-list" data-news-list data-news-max="4" data-news-keep="10"><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">4/5/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Praying for blessings at Kue Chai Tung Shrine, Phang Nga Province</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> · NBT2HD</span><a class="news-out" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q6K2Zl6700I" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">13/4/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Phang Nga Hosts Grand Songkran, Alms Giving in Takua Pa Old Town for Thai New Year Blessings</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/traditions/">New Year's Dawn Almsgiving</a> · TOPNEWS</span><a class="news-out" href="https://www.topnews.co.th/news/1546452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">13/4/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Takua Pa Blooms! Retracing Old Town Charm at Takuapa Oldtown Songkran Festival 2026</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/traditions/">New Year's Dawn Almsgiving</a> · MGR Online</span><a class="news-out" href="https://mgronline.com/onlinesection/detail/9690000036775" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">8/3/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Takua Pa Khiri Khet School participates in Takua Pa Walk Rally 2026 (2569 BE)</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a> · Takua Pa Khiri Khet School</span><a class="news-out" href="https://www.keereekatschool.ac.th/gallery-detail_1497" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">1/3/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Phang Nga hosts the 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/museum/">Takua Pa Community Museum</a> · สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand)</span><a class="news-out" href="https://radiothailand.prd.go.th/th/content/category/detail/id/9/iid/481052" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">21/2/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a> · YOUPHUKET</span><a class="news-out" href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">30/1/2569</span><span class="news-main"><b>Inviting check-ins at Boon Soong iron bridge, mining heritage of Takua Pa town</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a> · NBT2HD</span><a class="news-out" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QUZ54DTc0LQ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li><li class="news-row"><span class="news-date">5/11/2568</span><span class="news-main"><b>Loy Krathong activities at Khlong Takua Pa and Khlong Bang Muang</b><span class="news-meta"><a href="/en/traditions/">Loy Krathong</a> · กรมทรัพยากรทางทะเลและชายฝั่ง (Department of Marine and Coastal Resources)</span><a class="news-out" href="https://newweb.dmcr.go.th/detailAll/81026/nws/258" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read original news ↗</a></span></li></ol><p class="small" data-news-updated hidden></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/news/">View all updates ↗</a><p class="small">Compiled from public news · Check schedule with organizers before visiting</p></div></div></section><section class="map-teaser"><div class="map-teaser-copy"><span class="chapter">Open the map / Then go out and know the city</span><h2>Which alley, which street<br><em>Has a story waiting</em></h2><p>From Yan Yao to the old town, open the municipal map and slowly look for the next destination</p><a class="button" href="/en/map/">Open the town map<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="map-caption">Uses the original municipal map image</span></div><a class="map-paper" href="/en/map/" aria-label="เปิดแผนที่เทศบาล"><img src="/assets/municipal-map.png" width="1358" height="1938" alt="แผนที่ท่องเที่ยวเมืองตะกั่วป่าจากเทศบาล" loading="lazy"><span class="paper-tag">TAKUA PA · TOWN MAP ↗</span></a><span class="map-compass" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></section><section id="places" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">03 / Read the town</span><h2>One city, many angles to know</h2></div><p>All 20 places, from paper to stories of the city</p></div><div class="explorer" data-explorer><div class="explorer-tools"><div class="filter-tabs" role="group" aria-label="หมวดสถานที่"><button type="button" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All <sup>20</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="temple" aria-pressed="false">Temples & Pagodas <sup>6</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="shrine" aria-pressed="false">Shrines & Vegetarian Halls <sup>4</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="heritage" aria-pressed="false">Old Buildings & City Traces <sup>4</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="park" aria-pressed="false">Parks & Public Spaces <sup>2</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="market" aria-pressed="false">Markets & Food <sup>3</sup></button><button type="button" data-filter="museum" aria-pressed="false">Museums <sup>1</sup></button></div></div><div class="explorer-status"><span data-place-count role="status" aria-live="polite">20 places to slowly get to know</span><span>Select image to read ↗</span></div><h2 class="visually-hidden">รายชื่อสถานที่ทั้งหมด</h2><div class="places-grid"><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดบรมธาตุคีรีเขต (วัดลุ่ม)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/"><img src="/assets/wat-boromthat.webp" alt="วัดบรมธาตุคีรีเขต (วัดลุ่ม)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">01</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></h3><p>White pagoda and the town's faith</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดคุหาภิมุข (วัดควนถ้ำ)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-khuha/"><img src="/assets/wat-khuha.webp" alt="วัดคุหาภิมุข (วัดควนถ้ำ)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">02</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></h3><p>Small details that invite you to pause and look.</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดปทุมธารา (วัดหน้าเมือง)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-pathum/"><img src="/assets/wat-pathum.webp" alt="วัดปทุมธารา (วัดหน้าเมือง)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">03</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></h3><p>Old ordination hall and waterway stories</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/"><img src="/assets/wat-kongkha.webp" alt="วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">04</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a></h3><p>Southern Thai style ordination hall details</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดนิกรวราราม (วัดย่านยาว)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/"><img src="/assets/wat-nikorn.webp" alt="วัดนิกรวราราม (วัดย่านยาว)" width="1000" height="726" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">05</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></h3><p>The temple and community memories</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="temple" data-name="วัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์ (วัดใหม่)"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/wat-sena/"><img src="/assets/wat-sena.webp" alt="วัดเสนานุชรังสรรค์ (วัดใหม่)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">06</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Temples & Pagodas</span><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></h3><p>Thai and Chinese traces in the same building</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="shrine" data-name="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/guan-yu/"><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าพ่อกวนอู ซิ่นไช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">08</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</span><h3><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>Red door and the community's faith</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="shrine" data-name="ศาลเจ้าปุนเถ่ากงอ๊า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/pun-thao/"><img src="/assets/pun-thao.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้าปุนเถ่ากงอ๊า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">09</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</span><h3><a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a></h3><p>Faith in the old port area</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="shrine" data-name="ศาลเจ้ากู่ใช่ตึ๋ง"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/kue-chai/"><img src="/assets/kue-chai.webp" alt="ศาลเจ้ากู่ใช่ตึ๋ง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">10</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</span><h3><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>A space for people's hopes</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="shrine" data-name="โรงเจในสวน"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/rong-jae/"><img src="/assets/rong-jae.webp" alt="โรงเจในสวน" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">11</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Shrines & Vegetarian Halls</span><h3><a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></h3><p>Traditions passed down through places</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/iron-bridge/"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" alt="สะพานเหล็กบุญสูง" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">16</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></h3><p>Iron structure connecting mining stories</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="กำแพงจวนเจ้าเมืองตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/governor-wall/"><img src="/assets/governor-wall.webp" alt="กำแพงจวนเจ้าเมืองตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">17</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></h3><p>A trace on the wall that tells the town's story</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="บ้านขุนอินทร์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/khun-in/"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">18</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Windows and balconies inviting a look into the past</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="heritage" data-name="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/tao-ming/"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">19</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Old Buildings & City Traces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>A building that passes on language and culture</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="park" data-name="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/phra-narai/"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">12</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Parks & Public Spaces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></h3><p>Rest area with stories of belief</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="park" data-name="สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/thung-phra/"><img src="/assets/thung-phra.webp" alt="สวนสาธารณะทุ่งพระโพธิ์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">13</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Parks & Public Spaces</span><h3><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></h3><p>Steamboat traces in the garden</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/riverwalk/"><img src="/assets/riverwalk.webp" alt="ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">14</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></h3><p>Food and life by the river</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/culture-street/"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" alt="ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">15</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></h3><p>Walking and reading the city through buildings and people</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="market" data-name="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/food-center/"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">20</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Markets & Food</span><h3><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></h3><p>Many flavors in one destination</p></div></article><article class="place-card" data-place-card data-category="museum" data-name="พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า"><a class="place-image" href="/en/places/museum/"><img src="/assets/museum.webp" alt="พิพิธภัณฑ์เสนานุชรังสรรค์ชุมชนตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="card-index">07</span><span class="image-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="card-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Museums</span><h3><a href="/en/places/museum/">Takua Pa Community Museum</a></h3><p>Preserving the town's stories together</p></div></article></div><div class="empty-state" data-place-empty hidden><h3>Haven't found this destination yet</h3><p>Try another search term or view all places</p><button type="button" data-clear-places>Clear filters</button></div></div><a class="text-link index-link" href="/en/places/">Open index and search places ↗</a></section><section class="section traditions-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="chapter">04 / Read the town</span><h2>When the city has an appointment</h2></div><p>Year-round traditions · Timing from the source documents</p></div><div class="traditions-list"><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">01</span><span class="event-name">New Year's Dawn Almsgiving</span><span class="event-period">January 1</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Activities in the traditions section of the municipal brochure</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/new-year-alms/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">02</span><span class="event-name">Takua Pa Governor Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">February</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/ruler-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">03</span><span class="event-name">Relic Procession to Khao Phra Bat</span><span class="event-period">Makha Bucha Day</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/relic-procession/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">04</span><span class="event-name">Phra Narai and Deities Worship Ceremony</span><span class="event-period">March - April</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/phra-narai/">Phra Narai Park</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/narai-ceremony/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">05</span><span class="event-name">Vegetarian Festival (Jia Kiu Ong Chai)</span><span class="event-period">1st to 9th day of the 9th Chinese lunar month · Usually September-October</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a> · <a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/vegetarian/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">06</span><span class="event-name">Chak Phra Festival</span><span class="event-period">Day after Buddhist Lent ends</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a> · <a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/chak-phra/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details><details class="tradition"><summary><span class="event-no">07</span><span class="event-name">Loy Krathong</span><span class="event-period">Full moon of the 12th Thai lunar month · Document mentions November</span><span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="event-body"><p>Related places: <a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/en/traditions/loy-krathong/">Read details from document ↗</a></div></details></div><p class="small">Check each year’s schedule before travelling</p></section><section class="food-feature"><div class="food-feature-image"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" alt="ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="food-stamp">LOCAL<br>FLAVOURS</span></div><div class="food-feature-copy"><span class="chapter">05 / Eat and shop for souvenirs in the district</span><h2>Know the city<br>Through another flavor</h2><p>Open the list of restaurants, drinks, and souvenirs<br>59 shops from municipal brochure</p><div class="food-counts"><span><b>32</b>Food</span><span><b>20</b>Drinks</span><span><b>08</b>Souvenirs</span></div><a class="button" href="/en/eat/">Find shops<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section><section class="about-strip"><span class="chapter">Notes from Baan Siwara</span><h2>The town’s story<br>That we want to invite you to know</h2><div><p>Takua Pa 101 compiles information from the Takua Pa municipal brochure, with sources and data scope for you to read further</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/about/">Get to know this guide ↗</a></div></section></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/" aria-current="page"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
