TouristAttraction", "name": "บ้านขุนอินทร์", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/khun-in/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/khun-in.webp", "description": "บ้านที่เอกสารอธิบายว่ามีสถาปัตยกรรมชิโน-ยูโรเปียนและสะท้อนความรุ่งเรืองในอดีต", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ใกล้สี่แยกหมอพิทักษ์", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8307319975, "longitude": 98.3633399749}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เป็นบ้านพักอาศัยของ ร.อ.ท. ขุนอินทรคีรี (ช้อย ณ นคร) แหล่งข้อมูลการท่องเที่ยวของชุมชนจัดบ้านขุนอินทร์ไว้ในกลุ่มโบราณสถาน/อาคารเก่าของเมืองตะกั่วป่า"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "รูปทรงอาคารสองชั้นเป็นองค์ประกอบที่เห็นได้จากภายนอก การผสมศิลปะตะวันตกและตะวันออกในรูปแบบชิโนโปรตุกีสประยุกต์ เป็นบ้านพักอาศัยของบุคคลสำคัญที่ฐานข้อมูล ONEP ระบุชื่อไว้"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เอกสารเทศบาลกล่าวถึงที่นี่อย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "บ้านที่เอกสารอธิบายว่ามีสถาปัตยกรรมชิโน-ยูโรเปียนและสะท้อนความรุ่งเรืองในอดีต"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/khun-in/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/khun-in/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/khun-in/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/khun-in/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Old Buildings & City Traces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Old buildings and city traces</span><h1>Khun In House</h1><p class="english">Khun In House</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">3 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="khun-in">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="บ้านขุนอินทร์" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8307319975, 98.3633399749 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8307319975,98.3633399749" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The district chief's house in a tin port town</h3><p class="era-years">Around 1917 (B.E. 2460); tenure context: 1921 to 1926 (B.E. 2464 to 2469)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>หลักฐานท้องถิ่นระบุว่าบ้านขุนอินทร์สร้างขึ้นราว พ.ศ. 2460 โดยช่างฝีมือชาวจีน เพื่อเป็นบ้านพักของ ร.อ.ท. ขุนอินทรคีรี (ช้อย ณ นคร) ผู้สืบสายตระกูลเจ้าเมืองและต่อมาเป็นนายอำเภอตะกั่วป่าระหว่าง พ.ศ. 2464 ถึง 2469 จึงไม่ใช่เพียงอาคารสวยงาม แต่เป็นบ้านของผู้มีบทบาทในโครงสร้างการปกครองเมืองช่วงปลายยุคเจ้าเมืองสู่ระบบอำเภอ</p><p>The house emerged in Takua Pa as the town grew through trade and tin mining. Rivers and canals served as transport routes, trading boats from China and Burma exchanged goods, and many Thai people of Chinese and Hokkien Chinese descent settled here. Its two-storey adapted Sino-Portuguese brick-and-mortar architecture reflects both the owner's status and the Andaman trading world that connected Takua Pa with people of many cultures.</p><p>At that time, the house served as a residence for a senior official and formed part of an old-town landscape of merchant homes, shops, and religious sites. However, no primary document has been found that directly records its construction date, the craftsmen's names, or any other public function of the house.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Our Takua Pa: Tuek Khun In (Khun In Building)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Khun In Building</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a family home to an old town heritage</h3><p class="era-years">1981 (พ.ศ. 2524) to before 2026 (พ.ศ. 2569)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>After several decades of use, the building deteriorated. The Na Nakhon family repaired it around 1981 (พ.ศ. 2524), largely retaining its original form and replacing turtle-back roof tiles with corrugated tiles. Among accessible sources, this is the conservation event for Khun In House with the clearest year.</p><p>Meanwhile, Takua Pa changed from a mining and water-trade centre into a quieter town as its former economy declined. Rivers and canals became shallow due to mining activity, and the old community gradually took on a cultural and tourism role. Khun In House is therefore remembered alongside the cultural street, Chinese-European buildings, and evidence of the former mining town.</p><p>ONEP's official sources classify Khun In House as an architectural art site, while the SAC community database lists it among Takua Pa's historical sites. However, a review of accessible sources found no year confirming registration as a Fine Arts Department historic site, no record of use for another business, and no evidence that the house was damaged by the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547).</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Our Takua Pa: Tuek Khun In (Khun In Building)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A heritage building still under family care</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The status verified in 2026 (พ.ศ. 2569) is that Khun In House continues to be described as a historic building in Takua Pa old town. Local sources state that it remains under the care of the Na Nakhon family. The building's value lies in its adapted Sino-Portuguese style and its historical link to Khun Intharakhiri.</p><p>The house has no public information verifying opening hours, admission fees, an on-site caretaker, or official access to the interior. It should therefore be treated as a building that can be viewed in its external context, while interior access remains unknown. It should not be described as a museum or a regular event venue.</p><p>Today, the house has a symbolic role in the old-town landscape, alongside the cultural road and other historic community buildings. Unlike projects with clear announcements, no news or announcement from 2022 to 2026 (B.E. 2565 to 2569) has been found that identifies restoration or activities specifically for Ban Khun In.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Our Takua Pa: Tuek Khun In (Khun In Building)</a> · <a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097133" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TAT Media Assets: Phang-nga-Khun Intra Building</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">1917 (พ.ศ. 2460)</p><h3>Construction of Khun In house</h3><p>Built around 1917 by Chinese craftsmen as the residence of Khun Intharakhiri (Choi na Nakhon).</p><a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">1921 (พ.ศ. 2464)</p><h3>Khun Intharakhiri served as district chief</h3><p>Between 1921 and 1926, the house was connected to the person holding the position of Takua Pa district chief.</p><a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">1981 (พ.ศ. 2524)</p><h3>Major repair</h3><p>The na Nakhon family repaired the building according to its original style and changed the roofing material to corrugated tiles.</p><a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">10 September 2018 (พ.ศ. 2561)</p><h3>ONEP recorded it as an art and cultural site</h3><p>The ONEP database listed the Khun In building under the category of museums, architecture, and palaces, and noted the date of data modification.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>No readable evidence found regarding Fine Arts Department historical site registration</h3><p>The registration year or status with the Fine Arts Department should not be stated until official documents verify it.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Two-story building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The two-story building structure is a visible element from the outside.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Applied Sino-Portuguese style</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>A blend of Western and Eastern art in the applied Sino-Portuguese style.</p><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097133" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Historical house of Khun Intharakhiri</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It was the residence of an important figure named in the ONEP database.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the old town area featuring several historic buildings and cultural sites.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Khun In House is connected to Khun Intharakhiri (Choi Na Nakhon), who was a nephew of Phraya Senanuchit, the Takua Pa governor.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>The original roof of the building used tiles shaped like a tortoise shell, before being replaced with corrugated tiles during the repair in 1981.</p><a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town area, near the Mor Phithak intersection; accessible sources do not specify official routes or distances from a starting point.</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Sena Nucharangsan <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa Old Town <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa governor's residence <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Wat Khiri Khet <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>Ban Khun In can be viewed only from outside. To see what the inside of an old wooden house in this town looks like, another house in the old market area is open as a café.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Another wooden house you can enter ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>It was the residence of Captain Khun Intharakhiri (Choi Na Nakhon). Community tourism sources classify Khun In House among Takua Pa's historic sites and old buildings.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Its two-storey form is visible from outside. Its adapted Sino-Portuguese style blends Western and Eastern art, and it was the residence of a notable person named in the ONEP database.</p></details><details><summary>How the municipality document mentions this place</summary><p>A house described in documents as having Sino-European architecture and reflecting past prosperity</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Khun In Building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tourism Authority of Thailand (TAT): TAT Media Assets</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097133" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace: Khun In Building, Takua Pa, Phang Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Our Takua Pa: Tuek Khun In (Khun In Building)</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://kuapa.com/%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B6%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%8C/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets: Phang-nga-Khun Intra Building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097133" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace: Khun In Building, Phang Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960254" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Exact opening and closing hours: Sources only indicate that the opening hours are unknown.</li><li>Admission fee.</li><li>Official phone number, Facebook page, website, and LINE account.</li><li>Routes and distances from Phuket, Khao Lak, and the airport.</li><li>Construction year and builder verified by official or academic sources.</li><li>The specific role of this house during the tin mining era.</li><li>Registration as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>Parking, restrooms, and accessibility for the elderly or wheelchairs.</li><li>Festivals or activities held directly at Khun In House.</li><li>Walking distances to nearby locations.</li><li>The exact date and year of construction confirmed by official documents; local sources only state around 1917.</li><li>The names of the craftsmen or the construction company.</li><li>The role of the house other than a residence, and its ownership history after the original owner.</li><li>Impact from the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>The year and registration number as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>The operational status of the interior, on-site caretakers, opening hours, admission fees, and permitted interior visits.</li><li>The latest structural condition and restoration or development projects in the last 5 years.</li><li>Past news within 5 years that directly mentions Khun In House.</li><li>Original image files and permission conditions from online sources.</li><li>Original image files and image-use permission terms from online sources</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\tao-ming\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Tao Ming School · Takuapa old town · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="A school building that tells a story of cultural transmission · Tao Ming School Takuapa · Chinese school Takuapa · Sino-Portuguese Takuapa"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Tao Ming School · Takuapa old town"><meta property="og:description" content="A school building that tells a story of cultural transmission · Tao Ming School Takuapa · Chinese school Takuapa · Sino-Portuguese Takuapa"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/tao-ming.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/tao-ming.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง · อาคารเต้าหมิง ตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "โรงเรียนเต้าหมิง", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/tao-ming.webp", "description": "เกิดจากความร่วมมือของชาวจีนในตะกั่วป่าเพื่อการเรียนภาษาและวัฒนธรรมจีน", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า (ไม่พบเลขที่อาคารจากแหล่งที่อ่านได้)", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8338139717, "longitude": 98.3649490347}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อยู่ในเขตชุมชนเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า บริเวณถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า; ใช้แผนที่นำทางไปยังพิกัดที่ระบุ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารสร้างขึ้นใน พ.ศ. 2465 โรงเรียนเริ่มขอตั้งเป็นโรงเรียนราษฎร์ใน พ.ศ. 2463 และเดิมใช้ชื่อโต๊ะเบ๋ง ตามสำเนียงฮกเกี้ยน"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อาคารโรงเรียนประวัติศาสตร์ที่ยังคงเหลืออยู่ในย่านเมืองเก่า สังเกตรูปทรงอาคารและหลังคามุงสังกะสีซึ่งระบุโดยหน่วยงานอนุรักษ์ เป็นหลักฐานของการจัดการศึกษาโดยชุมชนชาวจีนในเมืองเหมืองแร่ตะกั่วป่า"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/tao-ming/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/tao-ming/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/tao-ming/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Old Buildings & City Traces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Old buildings and city traces</span><h1>Tao Ming School</h1><p class="english">Tao Ming School</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">10 verified points</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8338139717, 98.3649490347 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8338139717,98.3649490347" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>From mining town donations to Takua Pa's first Chinese school</h3><p class="era-years">1920 to 1922 (B.E. 2463 to 2465)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Before it had a permanent building, Tao Ming School informally taught Chinese through private instruction. When the Private Schools Act of 1918 (พ.ศ. 2461) came into effect, the school formally declared its intention to be established in 1920 (พ.ศ. 2463), using the name “To Beng” in Hokkien pronunciation, before changing to “Tao Ming” in Mandarin pronunciation. The name conveys the idea of leading toward knowledge.</p><p>The surviving building was constructed in 1922 (พ.ศ. 2465) with funds collected from mining magnates and Chinese merchants in the old market at Yan Yao, as well as merchant networks from Ranong and Phuket. Another official source describes it as the work of a Chinese merchants' association that entered the tin-mining industry to provide Chinese-language education for Chinese children. The adapted Sino-Portuguese building with its corrugated-metal roof was therefore not only a school, but evidence that wealth from mining, trade, and Chinese networks was becoming a community institution.</p><p>At that time, Takua Pa was a trading and transport district connected to the river and sea. The town grew through tin, while Chinese people from Hokkien, Guangdong, and Hainan came as workers, merchants, and entrepreneurs. The school helped give the Chinese community in the flourishing mining town a linguistic and cultural foundation.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a> · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>When the mining town quieted down, the school paused, but the building still speaks</h3><p class="era-years">1977 to 2025 (B.E. 2520 to 2568)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Local sources state that Takua Pa's mines gradually closed from the 1970s, reducing the town's activity, while Tao Ming School ceased operations later. Verifiable official sources confirm only that “the school has been discontinued” and that the building is under the care of the Tao Ming School Foundation, Takua Pa. They do not specify the year it ceased operating or details of any change in ownership.</p><p>No readable evidence has been found confirming that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami (พ.ศ. 2547) or that it underwent restoration in any particular year. It should therefore not be concluded that it was damaged or repaired because of that event, even though the Takua Pa area has sites connected with tsunami survivor assistance and the old town has regained a cultural-tourism role.</p><p>The old town boundary document by ONEP indicates the boundary passing through Tao Ming School, and the community database of the Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre classifies the building among the important evidence of the old town. However, this search has not yet found a Fine Arts Department announcement directly registering the “Tao Ming School Building”. Therefore, the conservation status of the area is separated from the registration status of the building.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning (ONEP): Takua Pa Old Town Boundary</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>The original building remains in the old town, but it is no longer an active school</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The currently verified status is that the school has closed down, leaving a historical building under the care of the Munlanithi Rongrian Tao Ming Takua Pa (Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation). Therefore, it should be understood that "visiting the building" is not the same as "visiting an operating school".</p><p>The building is located on Thanon Si Takua Pa in the old town area and is still used as a destination in tourism media by the Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality), the Kan Thongthiao Haeng Prathet Thai (Tourism Authority of Thailand), and old town activities, such as the cultural street held in the Thanon Si Takua Pa area. The information found verifies the context of activities in the area but it is not verified that activities are regularly held inside the building.</p><p>The condition verified from official sources is that the building remains and has architectural value in applied Sino-Portuguese style. As for opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access, wheelchair accessibility, and the 2026 (2569 BE) restoration project, there is still no verifiable public information. Therefore, one should contact the caretaker or municipality before traveling.</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</a> · <a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tourism Authority of Thailand: TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</a> · <a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building (location introduction video)</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1920 (2463 BE)</p><h3>Application for Toh Beng Private School</h3><p>The Chinese school, initially operated informally by private individuals, applied for private school status following the Private Schools Act of 1918.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1922 (2465 BE)</p><h3>Construction of Tao Ming School Building</h3><p>The applied Sino-Portuguese building was constructed with donations from tin mining tycoons and Chinese merchants to provide primary and Chinese language education for children in Takua Pa.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1977 to 1986 (2520s BE decade)</p><h3>Decline of the Mining Town</h3><p>Local sources state that tin mines began to gradually close during this decade, reducing the town's vibrancy. However, this is not a verified year for the school's closure.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2020 (2563 BE)</p><h3>Municipality Releases Promotional Video</h3><p>Takua Pa Municipality published a video introducing the Tao Ming School building as an old town tourist attraction.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">21 February 2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School</h3><p>Press releases indicated the Old Town Storytelling event took place at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa. However, full details from primary news sources are not verified.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>School Closes and Foundation Takes Over</h3><p>The exact year of closure is not verified. Official sources state the remaining building is under the care of the Tao Ming Takua Pa School Foundation.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>Gallery</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">Present photos</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">Historical photos</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>Present photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-school.jpg" alt="อาคารโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Tao Ming School seen from the front, on the old town culture street<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>Historical photos</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง"><img src="/assets/photos/tao-ming-logo.jpg" alt="ตราโรงเรียนเต้าหมิง" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>The Tao Ming School emblem<small>Credit · Kua Pa Pho Project image archive</small><small>License · Cleared for this website</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Old yellow building</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>A historic school building that still remains in the old town area.</p><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Applied Sino-Portuguese style</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Observe the building's shape and zinc roof, as noted by conservation agencies.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Traces of Chinese education</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the Takua Pa mining town.</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-02-21 · YOUPHUKET</p><h3>Old Town Storytelling Event at Tao Ming School, Takua Pa</h3><p>Press releases reported a full day of activities hosted at Tao Ming School.</p><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>"Toh Beng" is the original name pronounced in the Hokkien dialect, while "Tao Ming" is the Mandarin pronunciation of the name 導明.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p>Tao Ming School was the first and only Chinese language school in Takua Pa according to accessible local articles.</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The building was constructed by Chinese craftsmen and features a zinc roof in the applied Sino-Portuguese style.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance was found from verified sources.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Takua Pa Old Town Community / Talat Yai (Big Market) <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located in the Takua Pa old town community on Si Takua Pa Road; use a navigation map to the specified coordinates.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The building was constructed in 1922 (2465 BE). The school started requesting to be established as a private school in 1920 (2463 BE) and originally used the name To Beng according to the Hokkien accent.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A historical school building remaining in the old town area. Observe the building shape and corrugated zinc roof identified by conservation agencies. It is evidence of educational management by the Chinese community in the tin mining town of Takua Pa.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Noyobai lae Phaen Sapphayakon Thammachat lae Singwaetlom (Office of Natural Resources and Environmental Policy and Planning): Rongrian Tao Ming (Tao Ming School) building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4420" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre): Takua Pa Town</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/951" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal: Takua Pa Old Town and its endless tales</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Readme.me: Hello Phang.Nga</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://readme.me/p/51787" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">องค์การบริหารส่วนจังหวัดพังงา (Phang Nga Provincial Administrative Organization): Takua Pa Old Town</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngapao.go.th/travel/detail/89" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tourism Authority of Thailand: TAT Media Assets · Tao Ming School</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1099396" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thetsaban Mueang Takua Pa (Takua Pa Town Municipality): Tao Ming School Building</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qn0Tb1GSiZY" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">YOUPHUKET: Press release for the Old Town Tells Stories event</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://youphuket.club/author/admin/page/58/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No building number or postal code found in accessible sources.</li><li>No official opening and closing hours found.</li><li>No admission fee found.</li><li>No official phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account found.</li><li>No verified information on parking, restrooms, and accessibility for wheelchairs or the elderly.</li><li>No information on registration as a historical site by the Fine Arts Department.</li><li>No information on individual builders found.</li><li>No festivals held directly at the school found.</li><li>Official image links with specified usage rights are not verified.</li><li>No year of school closure found, nor a list of administrators or teachers.</li><li>No verified evidence of ownership changes or use for other businesses after the school closed.</li><li>No verified evidence that the building was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No year or documents confirming the specific restoration of the building found.</li><li>No Fine Arts Department announcement directly confirming the registration of the Tao Ming School building as a historical site.</li><li>No opening hours, admission fees, regular caretakers, interior access permissions, parking, restrooms, or wheelchair access found.</li><li>No verified restoration or development projects for the building in 2026 found.</li><li>No old photos with direct file URLs and clear usage rights found.</li><li>Activity news on February 21, 2026, was found on a PR aggregation page, but the main news or official announcement could not be fully read.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
